      "created_at": "2018-11-08T11:44:35Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-11-08T11:44:35Z",
      "body": "Hi @DaneWiid1, thanks for taking the time to file this issue. We recently simplified our implementation of the \"privacy mode\" settings option. Specifically, turning this option \"off\" makes it so your accounts are always exposed to the dapps you visit, but this doesn't prevent the approval popup from showing if a dapp explicitly calls `ethereum.enable()`. The \"privacy mode\" settings option was only ever meant to allow users to continue to use legacy dapps that may be slow to update to the new API. However, if a dapp is already calling the new API, meaning their code is already updated to handle the approval popup, users will still see the approval popup regardless of whether \"privacy mode\" is \"on\" or \"off\". It should also be noted that this settings option is temporary: it will eventually be defaulted to \"on\" and ultimately removed altogether in future releases, making private browsing the only option for users.\r\n\r\nThanks again for reaching out. Let us know if you have any additional questions while testing.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
