      "created_at": "2019-01-02T15:28:27Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-02T15:28:27Z",
      "body": "If enabling or disabling Privacy Mode has no effect, why include it in the interface at all? The user has no meaningful choice, so the option should just be removed OR the behavior of the option should be made consistent with all the documentation that clearly says what the behavior should be.\r\n\r\nI agree with the original rationale behind adding this option and progressing toward making it on by default.  This gives dapp developers a chance to make the necessary changes and test them out.  However, if the option is going to be in the interface, it should give users a meaningful choice where the meaning matches all the documentation of what the meaning is supposed to be, in many places, that are not updated and show no sign that they are going to be.  I believe it would be significantly better to restore the original, well-documented behavior of the Privacy Mode setting. ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
