      "created_at": "2019-01-03T12:47:01Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-03T12:54:07Z",
      "body": "@wbt,\r\n\r\n> If enabling or disabling Privacy Mode has no effect, why include it in the interface at all?\r\n\r\nThis settings option does have an effect, just not a visual one: accounts are either automatically exposed to dapps if this option is disabled, or not automatically exposed if this option is enabled.\r\n\r\nAlso, as stated earlier, this settings option is purely temporary so legacy dapps can work for the time being, and was never meant to reduce user-facing prompts on dapps that already call the new API. Our privacy mode [blog post](https://medium.com/metamask/introducing-privacy-mode-42549d4870fa) also states that users may still see the prompt with the option disabled as dapps update proactively:\r\n\r\n> At first, Privacy Mode will be opt-in (and turned “off” by default). Even if you haven’t turned Privacy Mode “on” yet, we want to make it clear what’s happening under the hood, so you may start seeing the “Connect to this site” dialog as you use your favorite dapps.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
