      "created_at": "2019-01-04T03:13:01Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-04T03:13:01Z",
      "body": "> This settings option does have an effect, just not a visual one: **accounts are** either **automatically exposed to dapps if this option is disabled**, or not automatically exposed if this option is enabled.\r\n\r\nThat's what I expected, too, based on all the documentation and logical software behavior.  That's apparently not how the software actually behaves.  If the option is disabled, accounts are apparently **not** automatically exposed to dapps, and if the user clicks \"cancel\" on the popup the dapp apparently does not ever get the account exposed unless the user later returns and clicks \"connect.\"  \r\n\r\nThis disconnect between our and even your expert expectations of how the software *should* behave and how it actually *does* behave is the basis and trigger for my bug report (#5971) and apparently this one as well. ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
