      "created_at": "2019-04-29T19:13:20Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-04-29T19:13:20Z",
      "body": "So apps that *are* implementing the new API are stuck with a crummy UX, where the popup appears even though the user has explicitely requested not to see it, and the app has no way (that I can find) of preventing the popup from being shown, nor any way of anticipating that the popup is going to be shown.  It is an unavoidable, meaningless popup that is presented to the user for no explainable reason, and the app has no means of ameliorating the situation.",
