      "created_at": "2019-04-29T20:26:07Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-04-29T20:26:07Z",
      "body": "@dkent600:\r\n\r\n> nor any way of anticipating that the popup is going to be shown\r\n\r\nFor now, you can use `ethereum._metamask.isApproved` to know if calling `ethereum.enable` will trigger a popup to show. `ethereum._metamask.isApproved` returns a `Promise` that resolves to `true` or `false` depending on if a user has previously approved a given dapp. Also, \"privacy mode\" was never part of the underlying EIP and was added as an afterthought to ease the transition from the old API to the new API. Unfortunately, we're now in a difficult spot where dapps are split between the two. Ideally, \"privacy mode\" would go away entirely since it was never meant to be a longterm feature, negating the issue you identified above re: divergent logic paths / UX flows.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
